galahad: Percy, I thought your shame banished you from the Round Table forever. What gave you the courage to show your face around here again?
Thanks for the faith, Galahad. I'd received an omen that made me think I should come back, shame or not.
galahad: If you have received such a sign, then I suppose you are here for some large reason. What is your quest?
- (Make bad joke)
	set {convo_progress.galahad.madeJoke} = true
	To find the Holy Grail, and my favorite color's red, before you ask.
	galahad: ...
	galahad: What in the world are you talking about?
	Nothing, nevermind. Should've figured you wouldn't get it.
	I spent the last few weeks accompanied by a kingfisher. I thought it was a sign for me to come back.
	Can you tell me how things have been here?
	jump gettingUpdate
- (Make something up)
	Nothing! I just thought it'd be nice to visit my cousin.
	Viktor: Something about their relationship could be made into a social puzzle piece - "our shared heritage"?
	galahad: Cousins by blood we may be, but I cannot fathom myself a soulful relation of a deserter.
	- (Explain yourself and argue)
		(Vik doesn't feel like writing this rn)
	- (Don't acknowledge that.)
		It's still nice to see you. How have things been here?
- (Just tell the truth) | [if {convo_progress.bedivere.bedivereGreeted} == true]
	Not sure, actually. I kept seeing a kingfisher and I figured it was time for me to come back. Has something happened in my absence?
	jump gettingUpdate
label gettingUpdate
galahad: Stagnant. Everyone has the same problems they did before they arrived, except for the new coat of paint. It's dreadful. (Something about how Galahad shouldn't be here, given his Purpose was fulfilled)
There must be something else keeping you here. You know the curse as well as I. (don't like this line)
galahad: That may be, but it still doesn't explain why you're still kicking around. I already finished your quest.
I guess there's something more for me. The kingfisher-
galahad: Yes, the kingfisher. Why don't you go look for it somewhere else? Some of us still have royal duties to fulfill, you know.
set {convo_progress.galahad.galahadGreeted} = true
if {questProgress.questingBeast.investigationStatus} != "galahadknows":
	[end_timeline]
else:
	- (Ask about the beast)
		Viktor: (Another place that could be used in a social puzzle?)
		I'm looking for a different beast, actually. I've heard that Bediwyr's having some trouble with one and you've seen it. Can you tell me about it?
		galahad: Oh, that thing. Yes, a strange one it is. It's quite large, actually. I can't imagine Bediwyr's incompetence that he is unable to catch it himself.
		I'm sure he's plenty competent. Maybe it's just a hard beast to catch.
		galahad: If that's the case, then surely others would have at least seen it. Not even Brunor has caught sight of it and he has cameras all over the hotel.
		- (Should I talk to Brunor?)
			galahad: I suppose you could.
			Where can I find him?
			galahad: Gods if I know. He works security now. I'm sure someone else could find him for you.
			set {convo_progress.Brunor.brunorLocated} = true
		- (Tell me more about the beast?)
			You said it was large, but how big was it? And did you notice anything else about it?
			galahad: I estimate it was about the size of a collie dog, large but not so large as that wolf running about. It was too quick for me to catch more of a glimpse.
			Viktor: (Unfinished dialogue branch)
			set {questProgress.questingBeast.investigationStatus} = "beastknown"
	- (Leave him to it.)
		[end_timeline]